  <!-- FROSTED FILM DEEP DIVE -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="frosted-title">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy with design</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="frosted-title">Frosted glass and etched-glass film</h2>
      <p>Frosted film is one of the most versatile applications in our range. It gives a sandblasted or frosted effect on glass &mdash; light-transmitting but opaque to outside view. Ideal for situations where privacy and appearance must go hand in hand.</p>
      <p>There is an important technical distinction. <strong>Etched glass</strong> is a permanent chemical treatment of the glass surface itself &mdash; irreversible and expensive. <strong>Frosted film</strong> (vinyl with a frosted finish) gives the same visual result but is fully removable without damage to the glass. It is therefore the practical choice for tenants, temporary arrangements or premises that may change use in the future.</p>
      <p>Applications we carry out most frequently: meeting rooms and boardrooms (full glass or an eye-level band), healthcare clinics and treatment rooms (full privacy coverage with logo cut-out), law firms (classic gilded effect using a vinyl technique), fitness studios and wellness centres (decorative patterns combined with business name).</p>
      <p>Materials we use for this: <strong>Avery Dennison etched glass film</strong> (premium, dimensionally stable), <strong>Hexis Skintac frosted</strong> (European, strong adhesion on difficult glass). Bespoke is standard: milled patterns, logo cut-outs in any shape, gradient effects from fully opaque to transparent. Maintenance is simple &mdash; safe to clean with glass cleaner, no special products required. Interior applications last seven years or more without visible deterioration.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

